        "timestamp": 1791855880
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=lcm_dvd#doc\">docs#lcm_dvd</a> with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Nat/ModEq.html#Nat.modEq_of_dvd\">Nat.modEq_of_dvd</a> as the bridge?<br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/Data/Int/Gcd.html#Int.lcm_natCast_natCast\">Int.lcm_natCast_natCast</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/GCDMonoid/Nat.html#Int.coe_lcm\">Int.coe_lcm</a> are probably also needed.</p>",
        "id": 631355571,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1791906987
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's really two lines with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.mod_lcm#doc\">docs#Nat.mod_lcm</a> (... weird name, but it does the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>→</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span></span></span></span> direction) and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.ModEq.of_dvd#doc\">docs#Nat.ModEq.of_dvd</a>, I just think there should be a single lemma that does this.</p>",
